ask(1793,'prompt-context','Redundant emotion updates and history growth bullet','Apply this supplied policy in order: accept scores ≥0.75; emit an update only if the accepted label differs from the last emitted label, initially none. Events are (neutral,0.80),(neutral,0.90),(sad,0.60),(sad,0.85),(sad,0.90). Which labels are emitted?', [('neutral, sad','The first neutral is new; its duplicate is suppressed; low-confidence sad is rejected; the first accepted sad is new.'),('neutral, neutral, sad, sad','That applies the confidence filter but ignores deduplication.'),('neutral, sad, sad','That emits the low-confidence sad or repeats an accepted sad, contrary to the stated rules.')],kind='algorithm_trace',difficulty='medium',ass=['Supplied deterministic policy, not source code; score equality passes; rejected events do not update state; no time expiry.'],steps=['Emit neutral at the first event.','Suppress the second event because the label is unchanged.','Reject sad at 0.60.','Emit sad at 0.85.','Suppress the final duplicate sad.'])
