ask(1798,'optimization','USB shared-bandwidth limitation','A supplied shared link allows 40 MB/s of payload. RGB uses 640×480×3 bytes/frame, depth uses 640×480×2 bytes/frame, and mono audio uses 48000 bytes/s. What is the maximum common whole-number image frame rate, with no overhead?', [('26 frames/s','The image pair is1536000 bytes; (40000000−48000)/1536000≈26.01, so floor to26.'),('30 frames/s','At30 the combined payload is46128000 bytes/s, above the limit.'),('43 frames/s','That approximately ignores the depth payload and budgets RGB alone.')],kind='numerical',difficulty='medium',ass=['All values supplied; decimal MB=1000000 bytes; uncompressed synchronized image pairs; audio fixed; no headers or bus inefficiency.'],steps=['Add 3 RGB bytes and 2 depth bytes per pixel.','Compute640×480×5=1536000 bytes per image pair.','Subtract48000 bytes/s audio from40000000 bytes/s.','Divide and floor to a whole image-pair rate.'],formulas=[fm('B_pair=WH(b_RGB+b_depth); f_max=floor((R_max−R_audio)/B_pair)',{'B_pair':'Payload bytes per synchronized image pair','W,H':'Image width and height','b_RGB,b_depth':'Bytes per pixel in each stream','R_max':'Shared payload capacity','R_audio':'Audio byte rate','f_max':'Maximum whole image-pair rate'},{'B_pair':'bytes','W,H':'pixels','b_RGB,b_depth':'bytes/pixel','R_max,R_audio':'bytes/s','f_max':'frames/s'},['Same W,H and rate for both images; decimal MB; positive available capacity; no transport overhead.'])])
ask(1798,'optimization','Inference speed and responsiveness bullets','A supplied emotion worker takes80ms per frame and cannot overlap inference. Frames arrive at30Hz. If it must process every frame, what is its service rate and long-run queue trend?', [('12.5 frames/s; backlog grows','The worker is slower than arrivals, so every-frame processing accumulates work.'),('30 frames/s; backlog stays bounded because the camera sets the rate','Arrival rate does not increase the worker’s processing capacity.'),('80 frames/s; backlog drains','Milliseconds per frame must be inverted, not relabeled frames per second.')],kind='numerical',ass=['Single worker, constant durations, no batching/parallelism/dropping and sufficiently long run; queue capacity not limiting the arithmetic.'],steps=['Convert80ms to0.080s.','Compute service rate1/0.080=12.5Hz.','Compare30Hz arrivals with12.5Hz service.'],formulas=[fm('μ=1/T_s; backlog_rate=λ−μ when λ>μ',{'μ':'Service capacity','T_s':'Service time per frame','λ':'Arrival rate','backlog_rate':'Unprocessed-frame accumulation rate'},{'μ,λ,backlog_rate':'frames/s','T_s':'s/frame'},['Single sequential worker; no frame dropping or parallelism.'])])
ask(1798,'optimization','Asynchronous synchronization requirement','At decision time10.0s, accept an observation only if score≥0.75 and age≤0.30s. Which supplied observation is eligible?', [('score0.80 captured at9.75s','Age0.25s and score0.80 satisfy both conditions.'),('score0.95 captured at9.50s','Its score is high but age0.50s exceeds the limit.'),('score0.70 captured at9.90s','It is fresh, but its score is below0.75.')],kind='algorithm_trace',ass=['Synchronized clocks; no future timestamps; inclusive bounds; confidence not assumed calibrated.'],steps=['Subtract each capture time from10.0s:0.25,0.50,0.10s.','Apply both confidence and age conditions; only the0.80-score observation passes.'],formulas=[AGE])
