ask(1794,'end-to-end','Parallel modalities joined as context; supported by later synchronization and prompt policy','At t=5.00s the user asks for directions. The latest visual observation is sad,score0.90,captured at4.40s. A supplied policy accepts scores≥0.75 only when age≤0.30s, prioritizes spoken intent and omits invalid visual context. Which response plan follows?', [('Give directions without asserting current sadness','The score passes, but age0.60s fails; preserve the valid spoken task.'),('Replace directions with a sadness-focused conversation because0.90 exceeds the score threshold','That ignores age validity and spoken-intent priority.'),('State that the user is neutral and then give directions','Rejecting stale sadness does not establish neutral.')],kind='synthesis',difficulty='medium',ck='figure',ass=['Synchronized clocks; supplied policy, not source implementation; no newer valid observation or other affect evidence.'],steps=['Compute age5.00−4.40=0.60s.','Compare0.60s with0.30s: observation invalid despite score0.90.','Omit inferred emotion and follow the directions request.'],formulas=[AGE],cites=[(1793,'statement','Spoken intent prioritized; contextual prompt updates'),(1798,'statement','Asynchronous synchronization')])
